Give `isolation` the -f flag that `prominence` in the same repo already has.

Upstream hardcodes `FileFormat::Value::HGT` -- SRTM 3-arcsecond, 1201x1201 --
with a TODO beside it asking for exactly this. Our tiles are 1-arcsecond,
3601x3601, cut from GEDTM30, so the unpatched binary reads every one with the
wrong stride. It does not fail: it reports wrong elevations at wrong places,
which is the kind of answer that gets believed.

The `case 'f'` block is copied from prominence.cpp so the two agree on what a
format name means. Worth sending upstream; until then this file is the fork.

  git -C mountains apply .../deploy/mountains-isolation-format.patch
